## 4. Conclusions
In summary, we reported the fabrication of Cu–BTC metal–organic frameworks (Cu–MOF) from molecular precursors by using the ultrasound technique. Cu–BTC MOF may indeed be suitable for applications requiring frequent loading and unloading of guests. The activated empty phase has excellent and promising rifampicin affinity, and it can be slowly delivered to ethanol controllably. Results suggest that the adsorbed quantity of rifampicin over nano Cu(II)–MOF is much higher than those over a bulk Cu–MOF. To verify the crystalline nature of the product, the XRPD patterns of the resulting product were investigated. From XRPD, it is clearly confirmed that the Cu-MOF particles were successfully prepared by the ultrasound irradiation method. Acceptable matches with slight difference in 2θ, were observed between the simulated XRPD pattern and the experimental data.
